A||||11||WampusCat||Lyin' fuel guage||||11||
Z||000000||WampusCat||01-25-2001||10:17 PM||||So I'm cruisin' down a busy street today with 1/4 tank of fuel indicated when the car starts to stumble and dies.  I get it started and it runs long enough to get over to a parking space then dies again.  It kinda tries to start on the next attempt but then just cranks with no lightoff after that.  Hmm... seems like a dead fuel pump.  Just being hopeful, I walk home and get the truck and swing by a gas station with a gas can for a couple of gallons.  Put the gas in, starts right up, runs fine.  Geeze, I guess those times I pulled in to get gas with a little over 1/4 tank "just to be safe," I was really probably running of fumes!  Any fixes for a really inaccurate fuel guage?<BR>Oh, My7Fieros, I guess it is only a 10 gallon tank.  I guess I thought it was 12 because it took about 10 to fill from "1/4 tank."<p>[This message has been edited by WampusCat (edited 01-25-2001).]||||reg||11
Z||000001||Coop88||01-25-2001||10:28 PM||||If it makes you feel any better, that happened to me twice. Sometimes the needle stops at 1/4 tank, sometimes it goes all the way down. Maybe it's the sending unit? I just use my trip odometer now. I haven't run it dry since. ||||reg||10
Z||000002||ray b||01-25-2001||10:37 PM|||| try cheap fix first pull gadge cover glass and see if pointer is loose on shaft,one drop of glue fixed mine after same situation, make sure your tank is full then put back on at full mark. ray||||reg||1
Z||000003||Hank is Here||01-25-2001||11:15 PM||||I have a pointless story here about running out of gas in a Fiero...not me though<P>This is about 3 1/2 years ago in August.  The 88 Coupe that I now have was my sister's car.  She had had it for about 3 years herself and knew the car and the fuel gauge. <P>Can you think of the absolute WORST time for a woman to run out of gas?????<P>Well my sister can.  About 1 1/2 hours before her wedding.  lol  I am in the house and had just put my suite on.  And then the next thing I hear is my sister come in the door crying her brains out with her dress in one hand and her maid of honor right behind her.  "My car just died" is all I hear. It happened out on the interstate and lucky enough some kind people picked her up and dropped her off.  Just to get away from her in the "great" mood she was in I volunteered to get the car quick.  I went and got our wrecker about a mile away picked up the car, and dropped it off at the shop in 15 min flat.  This is my speed record for picking up a car.  I told my echanic it just died and went home to change.  All I can say is the sound of a 454 and TH400 in reverse at about 4500rpm down the interstate is loud.  <P>After the wedding I stopped back at the shop and checked on the car, here she just ran it out of gas, still showed 1/4 tank.   The mechnic and I just laughed like crazy.  I still joke with my sister about it today.  <P>They did not rent a limo but just used my fathers 88GT for their get away car from the chruch.  <P>Just a totally pointless story, but still fiero related.  ||||reg||1
Z||000004||My7Fieros||01-25-2001||11:25 PM||||Yeah Wampus it happened to me to in my Formula....I now know to refill when it gets near 1/4 tank.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Oreif||01-26-2001||01:23 AM||||Mine does the same thing. I called a Pontiac Dealer and you can still get the sending units. They are $385.00!!!!!!! I just fill-up when it's near 1/4 tank or by the trip odometer.||||reg||1
Z||000006||RossT||01-26-2001||02:11 AM||||There is a fix, but you have to remove the sending unit.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.mn.org/Knowledge/Procedure.asp?Version=d48od76p&Catid=22&Id=46&Action=Edit" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.mn.org/Knowledge/Procedure.asp?Version=d48od76p&Catid=22&Id=46&Action=Edit</A> <P>There is also a good article in the most recent Fiero Owner magazine from FOCOA about how to test the gauge,sending unit and wires.<P>My gage does read high, and it also likes to peg all the way to the right from time to time.  The needle also likes to jump around as the gas sloshes around. I will be dropping my tank as soon as it nice out.||||reg||1
Z||000007||tgowens||01-26-2001||02:47 AM||||by the way, you have an 11.9 gal. tank.........||||reg||1
Z||000008||WampusCat||01-26-2001||11:29 AM||||Yeah, I just checked the owners manual and it says the capacity is 11.9 gallons.  But, yesterday, I ran it bone dry, put in 2.5 gallons from a gas can, drove 2 miles to a station and it only took 7.7 gallons to fill up.  I'll see if I can get any more in this afternoon, but I tried to get as much in there as I could yesterday.  weird.||||reg||1
Z||000009||2xsess||01-26-2001||12:36 PM||||Same thing happened to me, luckily I was trying to leave work for lunch and it wouldn't start. I figured it was just that I hadn't put the needle back on right after doing the white face conversion.<P>$385???!!?? <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"> are they nuts?<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>AOL IM : Only2xsess<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/My_car_(large)sig_1.JPG">   <BR> <A HREF="http://kresgeus.homestead.com/FieroPage.html" TARGET=_blank>http://kresgeus.homestead.com/FieroPage.html</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000010||DavidHenshaw||01-26-2001||12:40 PM||||My 86 GT has the same problem. Any reading below 1/4 tank is reason to pull into the nearest station no matter what they are charging for gas. After running out of gas in northern WVa after driving about 100 miles on back country roads,(thank God it happened in a town 2 blocks from a station), I wouldn't trust my gauge even if it was fixed. I just use my trip odometer now.<P>PS: Even with the gauge problem after owning the car since last summer I still can't get over what a wonderful car this is. My wife is so tired of hearing about it she's ready to scream.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000011||Black88GT||01-26-2001||01:51 PM||||Tip for new members.  Using the search function will 9 out of 10 times prevent you from posting about a topic that has been covered 100 times in the past.  <P>It's ironic because now that I am buying a fuel pump I was going to fix this problem that almost all Fiero's have.  So, I used the search function, and wa-la, I found an article Ray Paulk wrote on the Fiero Knowledge database or something like that.    <P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/cartmanico.gif">             <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kennyico.gif">           <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/stanico.gif">         <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kyleico.gif">             <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/chefico.gif"> ||||reg||14
